// Deal or Force - where a region's townspeople live, province by province (StatePartition).
//
// One question is asked of this table and no other: when a region is divided between two
// holders - a front line through an oblast, a faction's half of a governorate - how many of
// the region's people are in each piece. The townspeople are shared by these weights, the
// country people by the ground each piece covers. Only shares within one region are taken, so
// the unit does not matter; these are people.
//
//   provinces     how many provinces the map had when this was measured. A table measured on
//                 another map is not read: its numbers would land on the wrong provinces.
//   townspeople   province id -> weight. A province not listed has no towns.
//
// This is a property of the map's provinces, not of the cities: a city in map_data/cities is a
// name and a place and nothing else. The figures were summed once, on 16 November 2026, from the
// urban-area sizes the city list used to carry (Natural Earth, public domain), so that the
// countries that open the 2024 world already divided - Ukraine, Syria, Yemen, Sudan, Myanmar,
// Libya, DR Congo - open with the people they had. Later files in this folder win, province by
// province. A map with no table here counts every city standing in a province as one.
